From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 17:22:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Storyboard every video engine, not just topic mode
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Patch 12 gave topic videos a storyboard to review before rendering, but it
only paused when the visuals were AI stills or a locked character — and the
studio defaults topic videos to stock footage, so most people never saw one.
The other three engines never planned at all.

Now every engine that plans something worth looking at pauses on it:

  text_to_video   a shot list of 1-5 shots, split from the brief by the LLM
                  and joined back into one video after rendering
  image_to_video  the uploaded photo, with what it should do and for how long
  slideshow       every photo with its own caption and hold time
  topic_to_video  unchanged, minus the toggle being hidden on stock footage

Scene lengths are editable wherever nothing has been voiced yet — a clip
holds 3-10s, a slide 1-10s — and pinned to the recording where narration
already exists. Only generated stills offer a redraw; a slide or photo
preview is the user's own upload and a shot list has no still at all.

Multi-shot clips are priced per shot at enqueue, so declining review still
renders the shots that were paid for. Nothing beyond the reservation is
metered until the plan is approved, and an unapproved plan is swept and
refunded after a day, exactly as before.

The review itself is now a dialog that opens as soon as the plan lands, with
an Open storyboard button to get it back after a dismissal. Render flushes
whatever is on screen before it starts, so an edit that was typed but not
saved is never filmed without.

